      "label": "section_header",
      "level": 2,
      "meta": null,
      "orig": "Q: We’re a SaaS startup with a three-person team. We’re at a stage now where we’re onboarding a few new customers per week and things are picking up. When you were building Localmind – at what point did you put your foot down on the hiring? We’ve raised some angel money before but not sure when it’s right to raise more. We want to move as fast as possible but don’t want to risk quadrupling the burn rate only to run out of money. It would be great to know your thoughts and what you would suggest regarding the right timing on growing the team and balancing speed vs cost.",
      "parent": {
        "$ref": "#/body"
      },
      "prov": [],
      "self_ref": "#/texts/8",
      "text": "Q: We’re a SaaS startup with a three-person team. We’re at a stage now where we’re onboarding a few new customers per week and things are picking up. When you were building Localmind – at what point did you put your foot down on the hiring? We’ve raised some angel money before but not sure when it’s right to raise more. We want to move as fast as possible but don’t want to risk quadrupling the burn rate only to run out of money. It would be great to know your thoughts and what you would suggest regarding the right timing on growing the team and balancing speed vs cost."
    },
    {
      "children": [],
      "content_layer": "body",
      "formatting": null,
      "hyperlink": null,
      "label": "text",
      "meta": null,
      "orig": "At Localmind, we never got anywhere near to this stage (late 2000’s consumer social, location, mobile-based businesses FTW 🥴), but there’s a fairly clear guideline for when any business should raise meaningful money, start hiring, and focus on growth: after you’ve found",
      "parent": {
        "$ref": "#/groups/1"
      },
      "prov": [],
      "self_ref": "#/texts/9",
      "text": "At Localmind, we never got anywhere near to this stage (late 2000’s consumer social, location, mobile-based businesses FTW 🥴), but there’s a fairly clear guideline for when any business should raise meaningful money, start hiring, and focus on growth: after you’ve found"
    },
